<title>USA: TABLE-Collaborative Q2 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Collaborative Q2 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Three Months Ended June 30,</p>
<p>						  1997		  1996</p>
<p> Revenue				$4,458,869	   $6,842,221</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)		( 486,496)		287,712</p>
<p>   Net income (loss) per share     ( 0.08)		   0.08</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>   shares outstanding		6,384,362	    3,770,558</p>
<p>				    For the Six Months Ended June 30,</p>
<p>						  1997		  1996</p>
<p> Revenue				$9,037,153	  $12,144,437</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)		( 904,882)		343,677</p>
<p>   Net income (loss) per share     ( 0.14)		   0.10</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding			 6,363,466	    3,433,942</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said lower revenues for current Q2 reflects the fact that backlog goals were not met.</p>
<p>The company said current six-month results include a charge of $300,000, or $0.05 per share, for costs associated with negotiations (hence termintated) to acquire U-Gene Research BV.</p>
<p>Full name is Collaborative Clinical Research Inc.</p>
</text>
